🔹 Why do we need Builder Pattern?

When a class has many attributes (fields), creating objects becomes difficult.

❌ Problems without Builder Pattern:
Constructor Parameter Confusion
You must remember the exact order of parameters
Easy to make mistakes (wrong value in wrong place)
Too Many Constructors (Constructor Overloading)
If some fields are optional, you end up creating:
multiple constructors
This makes the code messy and hard to maintain
Optional Values Problem
If the user doesn’t have all details:
They are forced to pass null or default values
Not clean and not safe
🔹 Example Problem
new User("Aman", 25, "Delhi", "India", "1234567890");

👉 Hard to understand:

What is 25? Age? Salary?
What if user doesn’t have phone number?


